```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gradient_clipping_global_confusion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> output,data;for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/recurrent-models/models/gradient_clipping/global/outputs.npz"))output.emplace(key,value);for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/recurrent-models/models/gradient_clipping/global/data.npz"))data.emplace(key,value);n::ConfusionMatrix cm(2);cm.add(data.at("test_labels"),n::argmax(output.at("logits"),1));cm.save_svg("build/gradient_clipping_global_confusion.svg",{.title="Gradient clipping / global: held-out confusion",.labels={"Negative cue","Positive cue"}});n::save_npz("build/gradient_clipping_global_confusion.npz",{{"counts",cm.to_tensor()}});std::cout<<"Truth rows, prediction columns; "<<(data.at("test_labels")).numel()<<" held-out observations\n";for(const auto& row:cm.cells()){for(auto count:row)std::cout<<count<<" ";std::cout<<"\n";}}

```
// result_begin: markdown
Truth rows, prediction columns; 128 held-out observations
31 33 
26 38 
\image(figures/gradient_clipping_global_confusion.svg)
// result_end

Policy: coordinate.

The held-out accuracy is 0.5703 (cross-entropy 0.6794), compared with the last-value baseline 0.5625, majority baseline 0.5000 and marked-value oracle 1.0000. Flipping the marked token gives accuracy 0.5469; flipping only the last distractor gives 0.5469. These are fixed source controls, not additional training. The finite synthetic test pool and short budget limit conclusions about generalization.

All three validation epochs are plotted; the test pool does not select the checkpoint.

